{"time": "2026-06-08T23:06:58", "event": "post_written", "user_id": "e_mixed_emergent_drift_g001_a01_bd76136a_007", "post_id": "n4b22v8", "subreddit": "worldnews", "content": "The speed at which people repeat highly specific casualty stats from active combat zones is wild. We're seeing numbers thrown around hours after an explosion as absolute facts, when in reality, it takes weeks to actually verify anything in a war zone. People just grab whatever stat fits their narrative and run with it."}
