{"time": "2026-06-08T23:08:40", "event": "post_written", "user_id": "e_mixed_emergent_drift_g001_a01_bd76136a_005", "post_id": "hfve50u", "subreddit": "news", "content": "The constant US government shutdown drama is just lazy theater. Every few months it's the same panic about national parks closing, only for a last-minute patch to get signed at midnight. If a normal business ran its budget this way, the board would have sacked the management years ago."}
